On its own, the model [[Technical Nutrient]]. It can be melted and made into something new over and over without getting worse. Remelting it takes a small fraction of the energy of making it from ore.

The [[Navy Chair]] is the proof. [[Emeco]] builds it from recycled aluminum and tests it to last 150 years. After that it can be a chair again.

Now put it somewhere else. In a [[Tetra Pak]] carton it is 5% of the sheet, a foil thinner than a hair, bonded to plastic. Same metal. This time it is mostly lost.

The material didn't change. What it was joined to did.

See [[Monstrous Hybrid]], [[Juice Pouch]], [[PolyAl]]
